@startuml
!pragma layout smetana

title Operational authorisation lifecycle

skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor #F0E2D0
    BorderColor #A87A4A
    FontColor #1A1A1E
    AttributeFontColor #3A3A3E
    ArrowColor #A87A4A
    ArrowFontColor #1A1A1E
    StartColor #A87A4A
    EndColor #A87A4A
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FBF3D3
    BorderColor #C9A227
    FontColor #1A1A1E
}
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam DefaultFontColor #1A1A1E

state "unseen" as Unseen
state "held over" as HeldOver
state "authorised" as Authorised
state "denied" as Denied

Unseen : Arrived, not yet looked at
HeldOver : Parked pending a query
Authorised : Released to risk and downstream
Denied : Rejected

[*] --> Unseen : Book
Unseen --> HeldOver : Hold over [reason]
HeldOver --> Unseen : Restore to unseen
Unseen --> Authorised : Authorise
Unseen --> Denied : Deny
HeldOver --> Authorised : Authorise
HeldOver --> Denied : Deny
Authorised --> Unseen : Un-authorise [reason]

note right of Denied
  A denial cannot become an
  authorisation, and the reverse is
  also barred. An attempt raises an
  exception, because reversing a
  terminal decision is evidence that
  something went wrong rather than a
  correction.
end note

note left of Unseen
  A working state, not a record of
  fact. An operator may restore a deal
  here having looked at it and left it
  for someone else.
end note

note bottom of Authorised
  This lifecycle records a decision
  about a trade. It moves no version,
  and the trade's own state is
  unaffected by it.
end note

@enduml
